//! # What it is for
//!
//! [`crate::conformance::real_laws`] is the function a backend author runs to find out whether
//! their carrier is sound. Seven mutants in `conformance.rs` survived every test in this
//! repository for one reason: **nothing here implements `Real` and is wrong**, so the laws had
//! never been shown to reject anything. A suite that cannot fail cannot answer the question it
//! is asked.
//!
//! `Faulty<0>` is a faithful delegation to `f64` and must satisfy every law. `Faulty<k>` for a
